/// Chapter 47 of the guide, written from md-docs/reference/grammar.md by
/// scripts/docsite/guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page GrammarGuide(path: "/reference/grammar", title: "Grammar", description: "The WebFluent grammar on one page: keywords, declarations, render and imperative blocks, components, tests, styles, operators, precedence and literals.", layout: DocsShell("Grammar", chapter: t("nav.group.reference"), blurb: "Every keyword and where it may appear, the shapes of declarations, statements and expressions, operators and precedence, and the literals.", source: "md-docs/reference/grammar.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "names", label: "Names"), Anchor(id: "keywords", label: "Keywords"), Anchor(id: "declarations", label: "Declarations"), Anchor(id: "render-blocks", label: "Render blocks"), Anchor(id: "component-bodies", label: "Component bodies"), Anchor(id: "element-blocks", label: "Element blocks"), Anchor(id: "imperative-blocks", label: "Imperative blocks"), Anchor(id: "style-blocks-and-themes", label: "Style blocks and themes"), Anchor(id: "test-steps", label: "Test steps"), Anchor(id: "expressions", label: "Expressions"), Anchor(id: "literals", label: "Literals"), Anchor(id: "comments", label: "Comments"), Anchor(id: "layout", label: "Layout")], prevTo: "/reference/runtime", prevLabel: t("ch.46"), nextTo: "/reference/browser-support", nextLabel: t("ch.48"))) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("This page is a map of what the parser accepts: each keyword, each statement, and where it may be written. The other chapters say what each form means; this page says where it goes.\n\nHow to read the shapes on this page:\n\n- A `text` block shows the shape of a form, not a program to copy.\n- `…` stands for more of the same, and `|` separates alternatives.\n- A word in lower case that is not a keyword, such as `expr`, `Type` or `name`, stands for something you write there.\n- *Render block* means a block that holds elements and the statements that declare state: a page, a component, the `app`, a test, and every element's children. *Imperative block* means a block of statements that run: an action, a handler, an effect, a timer or a hook.")

        Heading("Names", id: "names").h2

        Markdown("The case of a name says what it is:")

        Table(caption: "Names") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Kind of name").header
                    Table.Cell("Case").header
                    Table.Cell("Examples").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Declarations and statements")
                    Table.Cell("lower case")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`page`, `state`, `for`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Elements, and the names declarations introduce")
                    Table.Cell("capitalised")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Button`, `UserCard`, `Todo`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Everything else")
                    Table.Cell("camelCase")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`draft`, `isOpen`, `saveAll`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("A keyword has its meaning only where a statement starts. Everywhere else it is an ordinary word, so every keyword works as a map key (`\{ action: \"approve\", type: \"a\" \}`), a field name and an enum case.\n\nA name the language already gives a meaning cannot be a program's own: the words a statement is written with (`state`, `action`, `let`, `if`, `show`, `match`, `style`, `on`, and the rest), the built-in functions, and the values `env`, `params`, `locale`, `dir`, `now`, `viewport`, `query`, `hash`, `theme`, `network` and `update`. Declared as a `state`, a prop, a parameter, a loop item, a lambda's parameter or a `const`, one is an `E118`. The names a handler brings (`event`, `e`, `value`, `key`) and the browser's globals are yours to use. A program's own names may be written in any script, Arabic included.")

        Heading("Keywords", id: "keywords").h2

        Markdown("Each keyword, and where it starts a statement:")

        Table(caption: "Keywords") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Keyword").header
                    Table.Cell("Where").header
                    Table.Cell("Starts").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`page`, `component`, `store`, `app`, `theme`, `type`, `enum`, `api`, `const`, `data`, `image`, `animation`, `test`") }
                    Table.Cell("top of a file")
                    Table.Cell("a declaration")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`state`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block, store")
                    Table.Cell("a value that can change")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`persist`") }
                    Table.Cell("page, component, store")
                    Table.Cell("a value kept across visits")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`derived`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block, store")
                    Table.Cell("a value worked out from others")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`effect`, with `cleanup`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block, store")
                    Table.Cell("code that runs when what it reads changes, and its clean-up")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`action`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block, store")
                    Table.Cell("a named imperative block")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`use`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block")
                    Table.Cell("access to a store")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`resource`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block, store")
                    Table.Cell("a request whose state the page shows")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`validate`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block")
                    Table.Cell("the rules a state must pass")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`socket`, `stream`, `channel`, `peer`, `worker`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block, store")
                    Table.Cell("a connection the scope holds open")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`every`, `after`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block")
                    Table.Cell("a repeating or a one-off timer")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`on key(\"…\")`, `on resize`, and the other page events") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("top of a page, a component or `app`") }
                    Table.Cell("a listener on the document or the window")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`head`") }
                    Table.Cell("page")
                    Table.Cell("tags for the document's head")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`if`, `else`, `if let`") }
                    Table.Cell("render or imperative block")
                    Table.Cell("a branch")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`for`, with `in` and `by`") }
                    Table.Cell("render or imperative block")
                    Table.Cell("a loop")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`show`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block")
                    Table.Cell("a block hidden, not removed, when its condition fails")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`match`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block, or a value")
                    Table.Cell("one arm, by a resource's state or an enum's case")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sequence`, `step`") }
                    Table.Cell("render block")
                    Table.Cell("a timed group of enter animations")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`slot`, `event`, `part`") }
                    Table.Cell("component, before its elements")
                    Table.Cell("a slot, an event it fires, a part")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`children`") }
                    Table.Cell("component")
                    Table.Cell("where the caller's block goes")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`style`, `transition`, `on`") }
                    Table.Cell("element block")
                    Table.Cell("styles, transitions, handlers")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`let`, `return`") }
                    Table.Cell("imperative block")
                    Table.Cell("a local, and leaving with a value")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`try`, `catch`") }
                    Table.Cell("imperative block")
                    Table.Cell("error handling")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`await`") }
                    Table.Cell("imperative block, or a value")
                    Table.Cell("waiting for a promise")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`emit`") }
                    Table.Cell("imperative block of a component")
                    Table.Cell("firing one of its events")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`expect`, `click`, `type`, `press`") }
                    Table.Cell("test")
                    Table.Cell("a step a test checks or performs")
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Declarations", id: "declarations").h2

        Markdown("These forms are written at the top of a file, and nowhere else:")

        CodeBlock(#"page Name(path: "/", title: …, description: …, image: …, image_alt: …, type: …,
          noindex: …, lang: "…", translates: Page, layout: Component(…),
          guard: expr, redirect: "/…", paths: expr, param: Type, …) { render block }
component Name(_ positional: Type, prop: Type = default, …) { component body }
store Name(scope: .app | .session | .route, eager: Bool) { store body }
app { render block }
theme Name { token: value … }
type Name { field: Type = default, … }        type Name = Other { … }
enum Name { case, case(part: Type, …), … }
api Name(base: expr, …) { settings  on request|response|error(x) { … }  endpoints }
api Name from "spec.json" (base: expr)
const NAME: Type = expr
data name: Type = "file.json"
image name = "picture.jpg"
animation Name { from { css } 50% { css } to { css } }
test "name"(data: { … }) { render block and test steps }"#, title: "text")

        Markdown("A `///` comment before a declaration, a prop, a field, an event, an endpoint, or a `state`, `persist`, `derived` or `action` of a page, a component or a store is its documentation.\n\nA store's body holds `state`, `persist`, `derived`, `effect`, `action`, `resource` and the connections (`socket`, `stream`, `channel`, `peer`, `worker`).")

        Heading("Render blocks", id: "render-blocks").h2

        Markdown("A page, a component, the app, a test and every element's children hold these statements:")

        Table(caption: "Render blocks") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Statement").header
                    Table.Cell("Form").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("state")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`state name: Type = expr`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("persisted state")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`persist name: Type = expr \{ in: .local | .session | .name  key: expr  version: n  sync: Bool  migrate n -> n+1 \{ expr \} \}` — a page, a component or a store") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("derived")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`derived name = expr`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("effect")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`effect \{ imperative  cleanup \{ imperative \} \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("action")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`action name(param: Type, …) \{ imperative \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("store")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`use Store`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("resource")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`resource name: Type = fetch(url, options)` or `= Api.endpoint(args)`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("validation")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`validate name \{ rule(args) \"message\"  custom \"message\" \{ expr \}  async \"message\" \{ expr \} \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("connection")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`socket name = ws(url, …) \{ send T  receive T  on message(m) \{ … \}  on open \{ … \} \}`, `stream name = sse(…)`, `channel name = broadcast(…)`, `peer name = rtc(signal: …, …)`, `worker name = spawn(path, …) \{ on message(m) \{ … \} \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("timer")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`every(interval) \{ imperative \}`, `after(interval) \{ imperative \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("key")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`on key(\"ctrl+k\", e) \{ imperative \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("page event")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`on keydown(e) \{ … \}`, `on resize \{ … \}` — and `keyup`, `scroll`, `hashchange`, `popstate`, `online`, `offline`, `message`, `storage`, `visibilitychange`, `blur`, `focus` — at the top of a page, a component or `app`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("head")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`head \{ meta(…)  link(…)  script(…) \}` — a page only") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("conditional")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`if cond \{ … \} else if cond \{ … \} else \{ … \}`, `if let x = expr \{ … \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("loop")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`for item, index in list by key \{ … \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("visibility")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`show cond \{ … \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("choice")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`match expr \{ .case(a) \{ … \}  loading \{ … \}  error(e) \{ … \}  ready(v) \{ … \}  else \{ … \} \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("orchestration")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sequence \{ step(after: \"120ms\") \{ … \} \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("set-up")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Store.action(args)` — a call, run once when the block renders") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("element")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Name(positional, prop: value).flag.flag \{ block \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("slot use")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`children`, `slotName`, `slotName(value: expr)` — a component only") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("A connection's options may also be written inside its block, one `name: value` to a line.")

        Heading("Component bodies", id: "component-bodies").h2

        Markdown("A component's body is a render block, and before its elements it may declare:")

        CodeBlock(#"slot                                  the default slot, placed with `children`
slot name                             a named slot
slot name(value: Type, …)             a scoped slot
event name(param: Type, …)            an event it fires with `emit`
part Name(props) { render block }     a part, called as `Component.Name`"#, title: "text")

        Heading("Element blocks", id: "element-blocks").h2

        Markdown("An element's block holds these, in this order, each optional:")

        CodeBlock(#"Name(…).flags {
    style { declarations }
    transition { property: duration easing … }
    on event(e) { imperative }
    slotName(params) { render block }      a slot fill, on a component call
    children
}"#, title: "text")

        Heading("Imperative blocks", id: "imperative-blocks").h2

        Markdown("Actions, handlers, effects, timers and hooks hold these statements:")

        Table(caption: "Imperative blocks") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Statement").header
                    Table.Cell("Form").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("assignment")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`name = expr`, `a.b = expr`, `list[i] = expr`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("local")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`let name: Type = expr`, `let \{ a, b \} = expr`, `let [x, y] = expr`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("call")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`f(args)`, `Store.action(args)`, `list.push(x)`, `navigate(\"/…\")`, `log(…)`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("emit")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`emit event(args)` — a component only") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("return")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`return`, `return expr`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("conditional")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`if … else …`, `if let …`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("loop")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`for x in list \{ … \}`, `for x, i in list \{ … \}`, `for n in 1..=10 \{ … \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("error handling")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`try \{ … \} catch e \{ … \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("waiting")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`await expr` — makes the action asynchronous") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("`let`, `return` and `emit` written in a render block are an error that says to move them into a handler, an action or an effect.")

        Heading("Style blocks and themes", id: "style-blocks-and-themes").h2

        Markdown("A `style` block holds CSS declarations, one to a line:")

        CodeBlock(#"style {
    property: raw css value               to the end of the line, a `;`, or two spaces and the next declaration
    property: {expr}px $token             a live value, a design token
    --custom-property: value
    &:hover { declarations }              nested rules, as CSS nesting writes them
    @media (…) { declarations }           and `@md { }` for a breakpoint, `@container (…) { }`
}"#, title: "text")

        Markdown("A theme's body is the same declarations, without nesting.")

        Heading("Test steps", id: "test-steps").h2

        Markdown("A `test` holds render statements and these steps, run in the order written:")

        Table(caption: "Test steps") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Step").header
                    Table.Cell("Form").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("check")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`expect \"text\"`, `expect not \"text\"`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("click")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`click \"name\"`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("type")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`type \"text\" into \"name\"`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("key")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`press \"Key\"`, `press \"Key\" in \"name\"`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Expressions", id: "expressions").h2

        Markdown("The operators, from weakest to strongest binding:")

        Table(caption: "Expressions") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Level").header
                    Table.Cell("Operators").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("1")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`..` `..=` (ranges)") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("2")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`??`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("3")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`||`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("4")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`&&`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("5")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`==` `!=` (`!==` too)") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("6")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`<` `<=` `>` `>=`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("7")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`+` `-`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("8")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`*` `/` `%`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("9")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("unary `!` `-`, `await`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("10")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("calls `f(…)`, fields `a.b`, `a?.b`, methods `a.m(…)`, `a?.m(…)`, indexes `a[i]`, `a?.[i]`, flags") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("So `1..n + 1` is `1..(n + 1)`, and `a ?? b || c` is `a ?? (b || c)`. Operators of one level group from the left: `a - b - c` is `(a - b) - c`.\n\nThese forms are expressions too:\n\n- `if c \{ a \} else \{ b \}`, which is `null` when there is no `else` and `c` fails;\n- `if let x = v \{ a \} else \{ b \}`;\n- `match v \{ .case \{ a \} else \{ b \} \}`;\n- lambdas `x => expr`, `(a, b) => expr` and `() => expr`;\n- spreads `...x` in a list, a map or a call's arguments.\n\nA call's named arguments (`due.plus(days: 3)`) are gathered into one map, passed last. [Expressions](/reference/expressions) explains each form.")

        Heading("Literals", id: "literals").h2

        Table(caption: "Literals") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Kind").header
                    Table.Cell("Written").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("String")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`\"text \{splice\} \{value:.style(option)\}\"`, raw `#\"…\"#`, block `\"\"\"…\"\"\"`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Number")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`42`, `3.14`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Bool, null")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`true`, `false`, `null`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("List, map")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`[a, b]`, `\{ key: value, \"Quoted-Key\": value, ...other \}`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Regex")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`/pattern/flags`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Date, time")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`@2026-03-14`, `@09:30`, `@2026-03-14T09:30Z`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Duration")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`250.ms`, `5.seconds`, `90.minutes`, `2.hours`, `3.days`, `1.weeks`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Money")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`€12.99`, `$9.99`, `£4.50`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Colour")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`#0F766E`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Enum case")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.name`, `.name(payload)`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Design token")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`$name`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Comments", id: "comments").h2

        Markdown("`// to the end of the line`, `/* across lines */`, and `///` documentation.")

        Heading("Layout", id: "layout").h2

        Markdown("A `.wf` file writes blocks in braces. A `.wfx` file writes them by indentation: a line indented deeper than the one before opens a block, and a dedent closes it. Braces written by hand still work inside a line ([Language basics](/docs/guide/language-basics#two-layouts-wf-and-wfx)). Statements need no separator; two on one line are separated by a `;` or two spaces.")
    }
}
